CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F133A1768760744
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                 G2/11
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURES CNetwork BBC TV Presentation:
OL,4,Cslow to embrace female voices
OL,5,
OL,6,FShe was not, as some think, the first
OL,7,Fwoman newsreader.
OL,9,FIn the early days of ITV, Barbara
OL,10,FMandell presented a lunchtime bulletin
OL,11,Fwhich was dropped after a few months.
OL,13,FThen Nan Winton read the BBC News
OL,14,Fbriefly in 1960 but fell victim to the
OL,15,Fprevailing attitudes of the time.
OL,17,FBy the mid-70s, there had been a number
OL,18,Fof women newsreaders outside London but
OL,19,Ffor network employing a woman was still
OL,20,Fseen as a gamble.
OL,23,APub: 06-Oct-2024Qpppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,134,120,200,300,0,100
