OL,3,GFEATURES CNetwork BBC TV Presentation:
OL,4,Cslow to embrace female voices
OL,5,
OL,6,FIt took a long time before a rough
OL,7,Fgender balance was achieved but other
OL,8,Fwomen came through the ranks as
OL,9,Freporters and newsreaders in the years
OL,10,Fthat followed.
OL,12,FWomen were also making their mark in
OL,13,Fother areas of factual broadcasting
OL,14,Faround the same time.
OL,16,FIn 1975 Sue Lawley was the main
OL,17,Fpresenter of the Tonight programme (the
OL,18,Fancestor of Newsnight) before she
OL,19,Freturned to Nationwide.
OL,23,APub: 06-Oct-2024Qpppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,134,120,200,300,0,100
PN,13306
SC,0006
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F133A1768760744
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                 G6/11
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURES CNetwork BBC TV Presentation:
OL,4,Cslow to embrace female voices
OL,5,
OL,6,FValerie Singleton also demonstrated
OL,7,Fthat she could leave her Blue Peter
OL,8,Fimage behind on Nationwide and, later,
OL,9,FThe Money Programme although she still
OL,10,Fappeared occasionally on BP on special
OL,11,Foccasions.
OL,13,FMeanwhile Barbara Edwards was also
OL,14,Fmaking history even if she was billed
OL,15,Fin Radio Times as the "weatherman".
OL,17,FSo with all this in mind, it seems
OL,18,Fsurprising in hindsight that it was
OL,19,Fstill unusual to hear women network
OL,20,Fannouncers.
OL,23,APub: 06-Oct-2024Qpppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,134,120,200,300,0,100
